---
/**
 * /terms — DRAFT written for the pre-release preview. Must be reviewed and approved by
 * counsel before launch; the draft notice stays until then.
 */
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { settings } from '../lib/site';

const l = settings.legal;
const email = settings.contact.email;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms"
  metaTitle="Terms | Evenmont"
  description="Terms of use for evenmont.com, operated by JITO LTD under the business name Evenmont."
  lead="Last updated: September 2026"
  draft="Draft for legal review — not yet approved."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply to your use of evenmont.com, operated by {l.legalName} under the business name Evenmont. Our services are
      provided under a separate written agreement, such as a statement of work; if that agreement and these terms differ, the
      agreement applies.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use of this website</h2>
    <p>
      You may use this site to learn about our services and to contact us. Don’t misuse it: no attempts to break its security,
      overload it or collect data from it automatically.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Services and proposals</h2>
    <p>
      Prices, timelines and examples on this site are general information. A binding offer is the written proposal we send after a
      Blueprint, with its own scope, price and terms. Odoo licenses are billed separately by Odoo S.A.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The content and design of this site belong to us. Code we write for clients is assigned under the terms of each client
      agreement. Odoo is a trademark of Odoo S.A.; we are an independent company and not part of Odoo S.A.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep this site accurate, but it is provided as is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses
      that come from relying on its general information. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Cyprus, and its courts have jurisdiction.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
